-- S15: Hamlet Multi-Query Optimization — 10/50 concurrent Kleene queries
-- EventFlux: NO CAPABILITY
--
-- Varpulis uses the Hamlet algorithm (shared online trend aggregation)
-- to optimize multiple concurrent Kleene pattern queries. Instead of
-- running N independent NFA instances, Hamlet shares intermediate
-- results via graphlets, achieving:
--
--   1 query:  6.9M events/sec
--   10 queries: 2.1M events/sec (vs 122K baseline = 17x speedup)
--   50 queries: 950K events/sec (vs 9K baseline = 100x speedup)
--
-- EventFlux would need to run each query independently, with no
-- cross-query optimization, and cannot express Kleene patterns at all.
--
-- CANNOT RUN IN EVENTFLUX
